From: Johan Alvarado <contact@c127.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] spi: spi-qpic-snand: keep snandc->qspi->ecc in sync with the ECC ctx

qcom_spi_ooblayout_ecc() and qcom_spi_ooblayout_free() read the ECC
configuration through snandc->qspi->ecc, but that pointer is only ever
assigned in qcom_spi_ecc_prepare_io_req_pipelined(), which runs on page
I/O. qcom_spi_ecc_init_ctx_pipelined() installs the ooblayout without
setting it and qcom_spi_ecc_cleanup_ctx_pipelined() frees the context
without clearing it.

spinand_init() calls mtd_ooblayout_count_freebytes() right after the ECC
context is created, so the ooblayout runs before any page I/O has taken
place. On a first probe the pointer is still NULL or stale; on a probe
retry it points at the ecc_cfg that the previous attempt freed.

A retry is easy to hit: on IPQ5018 the partitions come from the
qcom,smem-part parser, which returns -EPROBE_DEFER until SMEM has
probed, so the first spi-nand probe always defers and the second one
runs against the freed context. When the slab has already been reused,
qecc->steps holds garbage and

  oobregion->length = qecc->steps * 4;

goes negative, so mtd_ooblayout_count_bytes() hands that back as an
error. spinand_init() then fails with a value that is not
-EPROBE_DEFER, so the driver core never retries and the NAND never
appears:

  spi-nand spi0.0: ESMT SPI NAND was found.
  spi-nand spi0.0: probe with driver spi-nand failed with error -512
  UBI error: cannot open mtd rootfs, error -2
  Waiting for root device /dev/ubiblock0_1...

On a Mercusys MR80X (IPQ5018, ESMT F50L1G41LB) this bricked roughly half
of the boots, the outcome depending on whether the freed memory had been
overwritten yet.

Set the pointer when the context is created and clear it when it is
destroyed.

Signed-off-by: Johan Alvarado <contact@c127.dev>
---
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-qpic-snand.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-qpic-snand.c
@@ -407,6 +407,8 @@ static int qcom_spi_ecc_init_ctx_pipeline
 	dev_dbg(snandc->dev, "ECC strength: %u bits per %u bytes\n",
 		ecc_cfg->strength, ecc_cfg->step_size);

+	snandc->qspi->ecc = ecc_cfg;
+
 	return 0;

 err_free_ecc_cfg:
@@ -416,8 +418,10 @@ err_free_ecc_cfg:

 static void qcom_spi_ecc_cleanup_ctx_pipelined(struct nand_device *nand)
 {
+	struct qcom_nand_controller *snandc = nand_to_qcom_snand(nand);
 	struct qpic_ecc *ecc_cfg = nand_to_ecc_ctx(nand);

+	snandc->qspi->ecc = NULL;
 	kfree(ecc_cfg);
 }

